% Problem 35. Chace vol. II pl. 57 (photograph XIV, registers 1-2), PDF pp. 161-162; Peet pp. 70-72 (Pl. L).
No. 35
"{Go down I} times 3 into the hekat-measure, '3 of me is added to me; return I, filled am I. {Then what says it?}"
{"The doing as it occurs."}
\ 1      1
\ 2      2
\ '3     '3
{Total 3 '3.}
Reckon with 3 '3 to find 1.     % "Call thou 1 out of 3 '3." (Peet: "You are to divide 1 by 3 '3")
  1      3 '3          % Chace sets this column out on one line: "1 3 '3, '10 '3, '5 2/3, Total 1"
  '10    '3            % no tick; Peet: (sic)
  '5     2/3           % no tick; Peet: (sic)
{Total 1.}             % "dmd 1" in red
{"Example of proof."}
\ 1      '5 '10
\ 2      '2 '10        % Peet: 2/5 '5 is not resolved by the table into '3 '15; "some more direct table being used"
  '3     '10           % no tick; Peet: (sic), "A tick is omitted before '3"
{Total 1.}
% the next two columns and the "Making of grain" are in parallel on the right of the page (Peet: the heading tp n syty "doubtless refers to both")
  1      320
  '10    32
  '5     64
"Total 96."            % "dmd 96": the '10 and '5 rows, the answer '5 '10 of a hekat in ro (320 ro to the hekat); no row is ticked (Chace and Peet), so the notation would add the 1 row too; quoted
{"Example of proof."}
  1      96
  2      192
  '3     32
{Total 320.}
"Making of grain:"     % Peet: "amounting in corn to"; Chace fn 4: the word (ss) "may have originally read ssr"
  1      '4 '32 '64 hekat 1 ro     % Horus-eye fractions of the hekat: Chace fn 5, "Special hieratic signs for fractions of a hekat are represented in this translation by numbers in heavy type"
  2      '2 '16 '32 hekat 2 ro
  '3     '16 '32 hekat 2 ro
{Total 1 hekat.}       % "dmd hekat", "Total a hekat", in red
